# Surgical carve-out (2026-07-30, repo hygiene Stage 1 --
# reports/repo_cleanup_stage1_20260730T004010Z/): two of the final_revision_*
# directories above are the SOLE source for scripts/run_ir_evidence_audit.py's
# cutoff-robustness and baseline-fairness sections (POOL_CUTOFF /
# BASELINE_FAIRNESS constants); without this carve-out that script cannot run
# on a fresh clone. Track their small canonical tables/manifests/scripts (all
# well under docs/ARTIFACT_POLICY.md's "prefer << 10MB" guidance except the
# one file noted below), but keep the genuinely bulky regenerable
# intermediates local. See gitignore_exception_manifest.csv in the stage
# report for the exact file-by-file rationale.
!reports/final_revision_task1_pool_cutoff_20260715/
!reports/final_revision_task4_exact_baseline_fairness_20260715/
!reports/final_revision_task3_ranker_dependence_20260715/
# task1: keep tables/manifests/scripts/logs/validation/FINAL_REPORT.md; the
# 1.6GB outputs/ tree and two large CSVs not read by run_ir_evidence_audit.py
# stay local and regenerable via scripts/run_pool_cutoff_study.py +
# scripts/run_pool_cutoff_exact.py (both now tracked under this dir's own
# scripts/ subfolder).
reports/final_revision_task1_pool_cutoff_20260715/outputs/
# task3: same pattern (found 2026-07-31, fresh-checkout reproducibility pass
# -- tests/test_task3_ranker_dependence.py does an unconditional module-level
# import of scripts/run_coverage_and_dependence.py etc., which previously
# lived only in the gitignored reports/final_revision_*/ blanket pattern and
# was silently absent on any real fresh clone). Track the ~450KB
# scripts/manifests/logs/validation/tables/FINAL_REPORT.md/TAXONOMY.md; the
# 33MB outputs/ tree is bulky regenerable scratch and stays local.
reports/final_revision_task3_ranker_dependence_20260715/outputs/
# pool_cutoff_method_metrics.csv (~254MB, raw per-method-per-query, not read
# by run_ir_evidence_audit.py or any tracked test) and
# pool_cutoff_exact_pair_metrics.csv (~6.7MB, not read by
# run_ir_evidence_audit.py) stay local; regenerate via the scripts above.
reports/final_revision_task1_pool_cutoff_20260715/tables/pool_cutoff_method_metrics.csv
reports/final_revision_task1_pool_cutoff_20260715/tables/pool_cutoff_exact_pair_metrics.csv
# task1/tables/pool_cutoff_pair_metrics.csv (~68MB) IS tracked despite being
# above the soft 10MB guidance: it is the direct, sole source of the per-query
# n=17,532 structure-utility correlation and publication figure in
# reports/ir_evidence_audit_20260729T182949Z/ -- excluding it would leave that
# headline result unreproducible from a fresh clone. Revisit if repo size
# becomes a problem (e.g. move to Git LFS) rather than silently re-excluding it.
# task4/tables/ is tracked in full (~1.7MB total, no further exclusion needed).

